{"cuisine/jharkhandi-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/jharkhandi-cuisine","n":"Jharkhandi cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["East Indian cuisine","cuisine/east-india-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Jharkhandi cuisine is the cuisine of the Indian state of Jharkhand. Staple foods are rice, dal, roti, and vegetables. Common meals often consist of vegetables that are cooked in various ways, such as curried, fried, roasted and boiled. Many traditional dishes of  Jharkhand may not be available at restaurants."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"jharkhandi-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jharkhandi_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Red ant chutney","dish/red-ant-chutney"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Flavours of Jharkhand","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"flavoursandreceipesofindia-jharkhand.blogspot.com","note":"Blog dedicated to traditional Jharkhand dishes such as dhuska and chilka roti.","url":"https://flavoursandreceipesofindia-jharkhand.blogspot.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Oecophylla smaragdina","ingredient/oecophylla-smaragdina"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["East Indian cuisine","cuisine/east-india-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/3b/Chhapra_Chutney_made_from_Red_Ant_a_food_of_Baster_region_at_Aadi_Mahotsav_MG_8684.jpg/500px-Chhapra_Chutney_made_from_Red_Ant_a_food_of_Baster_region_at_Aadi_Mahotsav_MG_8684.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Sumita Roy Dutta","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chhapra_Chutney_made_from_Red_Ant_a_food_of_Baster_region_at_Aadi_Mahotsav_MG_8684.jpg","of":"Red ant chutney"}},"cuisine/catalan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/catalan-cuisine","n":"Catalan cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Spain","intro":[["Catalan cuisine is the cooking traditions and practices from Catalonia. It may also refer to the shared cuisine of Northern Catalonia and Andorra, the second of which has a similar cuisine to that of the neighbouring Alt Urgell and Cerdanya comarques, often referred to as \"Catalan mountain cuisine\". It is considered a part of western Mediterranean cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"catalan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catalan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":5,"links":[["Arròs negre","dish/arros-negre"],["Crema catalana","dish/crema-catalana"],["Mató","dish/mato"],["Pa de pagès","dish/pa-de-pages"],["Samfaina","dish/samfaina"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Catalan Cuisine","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Colman Andrews, 1988","note":"Landmark English-language study of Catalan cooking and its history.","url":"https://openroadmedia.com/ebook/catalan-cuisine/9781909808362","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781558323292"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Cephalopod ink","ingredient/cephalopod-ink"],["Cubanelle","ingredient/cubanelle"],["Cuttlefish","ingredient/cuttlefish"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Squid as food","ingredient/squid-as-food"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Lemon zest","ingredient/lemon-zest"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Goat milk","ingredient/goat-milk"],["Sheep milk","ingredient/sheep-milk"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Cucurbita pepo","ingredient/cucurbita-pepo"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Catalan cooking","count":1,"links":[["Andorran cuisine","cuisine/andorran-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/00/Arr%C3%B2s_de_Pals_amb_pollastre_i_poma.jpg/500px-Arr%C3%B2s_de_Pals_amb_pollastre_i_poma.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Consell Comarcal del Baix Empordà","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arr%C3%B2s_de_Pals_amb_pollastre_i_poma.jpg"}},"dish/adana-kebab":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/adana-kebab","n":"Adana kebabı","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Turkish cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Adana kebap or Adana kebab is a dish that consists of a long strip of hand-minced meat, mounted on a wide iron skewer and grilled on an open mangal filled with burning charcoal. The kebab is named after Adana, the fifth-largest city of Turkey, and was originally known as the kıyma kebabı (lit: minced meat kebab) or kıyma in Adana-Mersin and the southeastern provinces of Turkey."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-adana-kebab"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adana_kebab%C4%B1"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Turkish cuisine","links":[["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bici bici","dish/bici-bici"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Çökertme kebabı","dish/cokertme-kebab"],["Doner kebab","dish/doner-kebab"],["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["İskender kebap","dish/iskender-kebap"],["Kavurma","dish/kavurma"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Kuru fasulye","dish/kuru-fasulye"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Mesir macunu","dish/mesir-macunu"],["Nevzine tatlısı","dish/nevzine-tatl-s"],["Ntolmás","dish/ntolmas"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Piyaz","dish/piyaz"],["Qatlama","dish/qatlama"],["Rakı","dish/rak"],["Şıllık","dish/s-ll-k"],["Stuffed leaves","dish/stuffed-leaves"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Yayla çorbası","dish/yayla-corbas"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/cf/Adana_Kebap.jpg/500px-Adana_Kebap.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Garrett Ziegler","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adana_Kebap.jpg"}},"ingredient/sirene":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sirene","n":"Sirene","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sirene, also known as \"white brine sirene\" (Bulgarian: бяло саламурено сирене), is a type of brined cheese originating from Bulgaria. It is made from the milk of goats, sheep, cows, buffalo or a mixture thereof. It is slightly crumbly, with at least 46–48% of dry matter containing 44–48% of fat. It is commonly produced in blocks, and has a slightly grainy texture. It is used as a table cheese, in salads, and in baking."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sirene"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirene"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine",[["Banitsa","dish/banitsa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Filo","ingredient/filo"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e1/White_Brine_cheese_cubes.jpg/500px-White_Brine_cheese_cubes.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Иван","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White_Brine_cheese_cubes.jpg"}},"dish/chelsea-bun":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/chelsea-bun","n":"Chelsea bun","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Chelsea bun is a type of spiced bun that was first baked in the 18th century at the Bun House in Chelsea, London, an establishment favoured by Hanoverian royalty accustomed to similar pastries in their native cuisine. The shop was demolished in 1839."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chelsea-bun"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelsea_bun"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Currant","ingredient/currant"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chefs: traditional British recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatbritishchefs.com","note":"UK chef-driven recipe site with a large section of classic British dishes.","url":"https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/features/our-most-popular-traditional-british-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from British cuisine","links":[["Banbury cake","dish/banbury-cake"],["Battenberg cake","dish/battenberg-cake"],["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"],["Bread sauce","dish/bread-sauce"],["Carpetbag steak","dish/carpetbag-steak"],["Christmas pudding","dish/christmas-pudding"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Crumble","dish/crumble"],["Crumpet","dish/crumpet"],["Curry in the United Kingdom","dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom"],["Diges